<title>USA: US FERC approves Orange &amp; Rockland power sale plan.</title>
<headline>US FERC approves Orange &amp; Rockland power sale plan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Federal Energy Regulatory Commission Tuesday approved a proposal by Orange and Rockland Utilities Inc to sell its own electricity and other producers' electricity at market-based rates.</p>
<p>The commission allows utilities to sell power at market-based rates if the seller and its affiliates are not in a position to dominate the power market or transmission in their market area.</p>
<p>&quot;O&amp;R's market share of installed and uncommitteed generating capacity will not exceed levels the Commission previously has found to be acceptable,&quot; the commission said in its approval.</p>
</text>
